        strategy: {
          basic: 'Lead with your strongest suit. Spinners open up more ends, giving you more options â€” control which numbers appear on the open ends.',
          intermediate: 'With the spinner creating 4 open ends, suit diversity is more valuable than in standard block. Track which numbers are on the open ends and which are depleted.',
          advanced: "In partnerships, communicate through play: your lead signals your strong suit. With all-spinners variant, the layout becomes extremely open â€” the game becomes more about hand management than blocking. In the single-spinner variant, controlling the spinner's four arms is the key strategic battleground.",
          tips: [
            "Control the spinner arms â€” they're the most flexible play positions.",
            "With 4 open ends, you're less likely to be blocked, so focus on emptying your hand efficiently.",
            'In all-spinners variant, the game becomes very open â€” high-pip tiles become liabilities.',
            'Larger sets (double-nine, double-twelve) with spinners can create 8-arm layouts.',
