          deckDescription: 'One standard 28-tile double-six domino set. Each tile has two ends showing zero to six pips; every combination from 0-0 through 6-6 appears exactly once. Spinners (doubles played crosswise) may allow play on four arms; no playing cards.',
          suitDescription: 'Tiles are matched by pip value at the open ends of the layout. There are no traditional suits; each end value zero through six can connect to any tile sharing that value. Doubles (spinners) are played crosswise and may have four open ends.',
          rankDescription: 'There is no rank hierarchy between tiles; play legality is determined by matching the pip value at an open end. Spinners (e.g. 5-5) are played crosswise and can receive tiles on both ends. First player to empty hand wins in block dominoes.',
          dealPattern: '',
